    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Pierce-County/Instruction---Classroom-Support-Technician-1_R-14759": {
      "title": "Instruction & Classroom Support Technician 1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: September 22, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 255M-YN_CS_NPS - Instruction & Classroom Support Technician 1 Business Title: Instruction & Classroom Support Technician 1 Employee Type: Classified Position Details: The Opportunity: The Expanded Food and Nutrition Education Program (EFNEP) is seeking a motivated Peer Educator to provide nutrition education to limited-income individuals and families in community settings. With training and support, this role delivers engaging, research-based classes to youth and adults, helping participants build practical skills for healthier living. This position is based with WSU Extension Pierce County in Tacoma. Successful candidates will: Be confident and engaging when teaching and facilitating group learning activities. Build strong relationships with diverse communities and effectively recruit and retain participants. Demonstrate excellent organization, time management, and the ability to work independently with minimal supervision. Reflect the communities they serve, including shared or relevant lived experience Duties include, but are not limited to: Planning & Preparation: Coordinate recruitment activities and prepare materials for classes and events, including food purchasing and preparation. Teaching: Deliver engaging nutrition education to diverse audiences, adapting to participant needs and learning environments. Data & Reporting: Maintain accurate records, complete evaluations, and submit timely data and reports. Recruitment & Outreach: Build and maintain partnerships with community organizations and recruit participants through events, presentations, and outreach efforts. Additional Information: This is a full time ( 100% FTE), permanent position. This position is overtime eligible. Monthly Salary: $3,565 to $4,746 | Range 39 Steps A - M | Successful candidates are typically hired at the beginning of the salary range and receive scheduled salary increment increases in accordance with WAC 357-28 . In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts; training and development; and employee tuition waiver. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for Classified staff and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications Six months of full-time experience/training in the appropriate discipline; OR equivalent education/experience. Experience working with food and nutrition in an educational setting. Ability to work a flexible, yet structured schedule with occasional night and weekend shifts to meet the needs of program partners and grant requirements. Must have the ability to travel within targeted counties, including overnight (for occasional trainings, paid for by WSU). Reliable transportation (mileage reimbursed) year-round. Must have, or be able to obtain by time of hire, a valid driver’s license and meet requirements in accordance with   SPPM 7.10   and departmental driving standards.   Ability to obtain within 14 days of hire and maintain a current Washington State Food Workers Card. Ability to organize materials for classes. Preferred Qualifications Experience planning and delivering education to youth and adults in nutrition, family and consumer sciences, life skills, or a closely related field. Computer skills, including Microsoft office, Outlook, Zoom, data entry software, or willingness and ability to learn. Ability to work well with other people and diverse program participants. Ability to keep written or digital logs of activities and complete reports. Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship About Department - https://extension.wsu.edu/efnep/ Area/College: WSU Extension Department Name: EFNEP Location: Tacoma, WA 98418 Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Position Term: 12 Month Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Pullman-WA/Career-Consultant_R-15353": {
      "title": "Career Consultant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: September 15, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 1482-YN_ADMINPRO - Student Services Coordinator/Advisor 2 Business Title: Career Consultant Employee Type: Admin. Professional Position Details: The Opportunity: Within the Carson College of Business , as a member of the Student Engagement & Career Development team, the Career Consultant prepares undergraduate business students for successful careers through individualized and group advising. This role helps students explore career options, develop effective job and internship search strategies, and build the professional skills needed to navigate today’s workforce. The position supports students at all stages of career development, with a focus on upper-division and industry-specific preparation. The Career Consultant designs and delivers innovative, business-focused programming that reinforces and extends required career course content, providing intentional scaffolding across the student experience. This work helps students apply and refine classroom concepts through skill-building, employer engagement, and experiential learning. By integrating employers and alumni into programming, the role strengthens students’ understanding of industry expectations, expands professional networks, and connects coursework to career goals. The Career Consultant collaborates closely with employer relations managers to stay informed about hiring trends, industry needs, and labor market developments, ensuring career advising, employer engagement and programming remain aligned with workforce demand and employment opportunities.  Additionally, the Career Consultant leads and contributes to initiatives that enhance career readiness, supports recruitment and onboarding efforts, and collaborates across the College to advance student success. This position is ideal for a professional committed to student development, industry engagement, and creating meaningful learning experiences that prepare students post-graduation success. Additional Information: This is a full-time (100 % FTE), permanent position. This position is overtime eligible. Monthly Salary: $4,600 - $5,500 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts; training and development; and employee tuition waiver. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for AP staff and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications: Positions require a Bachelor’s degree and three (3) years of professional work experience in student services or related education/experience. Experience leading or directing the work of others. A Master’s degree in a related field may substitute for one (1) year of professional work experience. Any combination of relevant education and professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year‐for‐year basis. Professional work experience advising, coaching, mentoring, or supporting college students or emerging professionals in a developmental context. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to coach others in developing professional communication (i.e. resumes, cover letters, interviewing). Work experiences developing and delivering presentations, workshops, or educational programming. Demonstrated ability to build relationships and work effectively in a collaborative, team-based environment. Working knowledge of career development processes, job/internship search strategies, and professional skill development. Familiarity with career-related technology platforms (e.g., career management systems, virtual tools, or online career resources). Ability and willingness to occasionally travel, and work evenings or weekends to support events and programming. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in career advising, coaching, or counseling in a higher education setting. Experience designing and delivering career development curriculum or programs that complement or reinforce academic coursework. Experience integrating employers or alumni into student programming or learning experiences. Familiarity with career assessments and tools that support career decision-making (i.e. O*Net, Focus2,   MBTI , Strong Interest Inventory, Holland Code assessments, Strengths). Experience using career services platforms and recruiting tools (i.e. Handshake or similar systems). Experience using social media or digital platforms for professional networking, student engagement, or job search strategies. Demonstrated knowledge of business career pathways, labor market trends, or industry-specific hiring practices. Relevant professional certification (i.e. Career Development Facilitator,   NACE   Career Coach, Gallup Strengths Coach). Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship About Department/College/Area/ Campus - business.wsu.edu Area/College: Carson College of Business   Department Name: Carson Center for Student Success   Location: Pullman, WA Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Position Term: 12 Month Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
