    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/King-County/Shelter-Medicine-and-Surgery---Clinical-Career-Track---Open-Rank_R-15332": {
      "title": "Shelter Medicine and Surgery | Clinical Career Track | Open Rank",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: November 2, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 164-NN_FACULTY - Clinical Assistant Professor - Career, 165-NN_FACULTY - Clinical Associate Professor - Career, 166-NN_FACULTY - Clinical Professor - Career Business Title: Shelter Medicine and Surgery | Clinical Career Track | Open Rank Employee Type: Faculty Position Term: 12 Month Position Details: The Opportunity: The Department of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) in the College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM), Washington State University (WSU) seeks to fill a continuous career track (clinical track) faculty position in Shelter Medicine and Surgery for its established teaching program partnership with Seattle Humane.  This position will operate primarily out of the Seattle Humane (SHS) in Bellevue, WA. The successful applicant will be responsible for instruction of DVM students on clinical rotations in an established partnership with SHS. Clinical rotations primarily include physical exams, spay/neuter surgery, dentistry and other general practice procedures on community and shelter-owned animals. The faculty member may also provide support for the DVM students when they work in other Seattle-based community-health focused programs including the One Health Clinic and the Doney Coe Clinic . The successful candidate will join one other full-time WSU Seattle-based faculty member as well as engage with SHS staff veterinarians and technicians. The Department is open to novel position structures, including partial/hybrid appointments, which could allow for private sector or other activities. Specific duties will include (but may not be limited to); case management, student mentorship and evaluation, supervision of support staff, coordination and delivery of the clinical teaching services, rotation coordination with other staff and administrators at SHS and interactions with faculty and administrators at WSU-Pullman.  The successful applicant may have opportunities to participate in additional didactic teaching, scholarly activity, and academic service as desired. The distribution of effort between clinical practice, didactic teaching, scholarly effort and academic service/outreach is negotiable. Additional Information: Annual Salary: Assistant Professor: $140,000 - $150,000 Associate Professor: $150,000 - $160,000 Full Professor: $160,000 - $175,000 In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Successful candidates typically begin up to mid-point of the salary range. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for Faculty and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications (for all ranks): Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM, VMD) degree or foreign equivalent degree (i.e., BVSc) and have experience in shelter medicine, high-volume, high quality spay/neuter, public or academic practice; and be proficient in general medicine, surgery and dentistry. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate, cultivate a positive learning environment, work collegially and collaboratively with people from all backgrounds and demonstrate commitment and relevant ability to foster community outreach, access and engagement. Preferred Qualifications: Specialty training in shelter medicine and experience in teaching. Considerations regarding faculty rank will be determined based on the interests and qualifications of the candidate, as will, division of effort. Applicants for Associate and Full Professor must have a more substantial background in clinical practice and teaching experience. For more information, see the CVM’s promotion guidelines: ( https://provost.wsu.edu/documents/2023/03/vet-med-promotion-and-tenure-guidelines.pdf ).   Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship About the College: The WSU CVM is organized into five departments/schools, including VCS, Veterinary Microbiology and Pathology (VMP), Integrative Physiology and Neuroscience (IPN), the School of Molecular Biosciences (SMB), and the Paul G. Allen School for Global Health, each dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, and service ( http://www.vetmed.wsu.edu ) About Seattle Humane: Seattle Humane’s mission is to create a kinder world for pets and their people through impactful programs and support services. The state-of-the-art shelter in Bellevue, WA serves as a regional pet resource center, providing adoption services, a community pet food bank and support for pet owners, low-cost spay/neuter surgeries and veterinary care, dog training, youth programs and more. Our team values collaboration, compassion, accessibility, respect and adaptability. For more details, please visit: http://www.seattlehumane.org . About the Area: Bellevue is located in the center of the Puget Sound region, situated on 31 square miles of rolling hills between Lake Washington on the west and Lake Sammamish on the east, and is only 8 miles east of Seattle. The city offers breathtaking views of picturesque sunsets on the water and snow-capped mountains to the east and west. Bellevue is the second largest city in King County and the fifth largest in the state.  For more details go to, http://www.bellevuechamber.org . About WSU : Washington State University is a land-grant institution with an enrollment of approximately 20,000 students on the Pullman campus and 25,000 students system-wide, including Spokane, Tri-Cities, Everett, Vancouver and Global Campus. The university’s web page, www.wsu.edu , offers information about WSU and the surrounding area. Area/College: College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM) Department Name: College of Veterinary Clinical Sciences (VCS) -- Shelter Medicine and Surgery Location: This position will operate primarily out of the Seattle Humane (SHS) in Bellevue, WA Application Instructions: Initial applications will be reviewed beginning September 30, 2026. Review of applications will remain ongoing until the posting close date of November 2, 2026. Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Curriculum Vitae 2) Cover Letter summarizing qualifications, stating the desired faculty rank and providing a summary of clinical, teaching, scholarly, and outreach and community engagement interests and goals Contact information including email address and phone number for three (3) professional references will be requested in the application. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Katie Kuehl, Chair of the Search Committee, by email (k.kuehl@wsu.edu).   External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Pullman-WA/Teaching-Assistant-Professor---Career-Track---Psychology--Pullman--WA-_R-15330": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor - Career Track | Psychology (Pullman, WA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: January 15, 2027 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 158-NN_FACULTY - Teaching Assistant Professor - Career, 396-NN_FACULTY - New Teaching Track - Pre-Academic Year Business Title: Teaching Assistant Professor - Career Track | Psychology (Pullman, WA) Employee Type: Faculty (+) (Fixed Term) Position Term: 9 Month - Summer Position Details: The Department of Psychology at Washington State University invites applications for an Assistant Professor (Teaching sub-track), Career Track faculty position in Pullman, WA, with a specialty in psychological science. We seek applicants who can make a strong contribution to undergraduate education in psychology, including regular teaching of our Introduction to Psychology course.  This position is a fixed-term, 9-month, 3-year appointment with the possibility of renewal. You will be expected to teach in-person classes on the Pullman campus, but may be asked to occasionally teach online classes as needed. You will also make service contributions to the department, college, university, and profession. The duties ratio for this position is 80% teaching (24 credit hours per year) and 20% service. It is anticipated that the successful candidate will begin the appointment on August 16, 2027. Additional Information: This is a full-time (100% FTE) , temporary, 9-month, teaching career-track  faculty position. This position is   not eligible for overtime . This position works  on-site/in-person at the WSU campus in Pullman, WA.  9-Month Academic Salary: $60,000 to $67,000 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Successful candidates typically begin up to mid-point of the salary range. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits for Faculty and AP staff and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate in any area of psychology by appointment start date . Proven or potential for successful teaching and instruction . Demonstrated record of or potential to effectively teach and mentor students at the undergraduate level. Demonstrated record of supporting, or potential to support, access and opportunity in teaching and service in alignment with WSU’s land grant mission. Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship. Area/College: College of Arts & Sciences Department Name: Department of Psychology Location: Pullman, WA Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. A cover letter addressing qualifications for this position as well as a response to the following prompt: ​ * As a land-grant university, WSU has a commitment to ensure access and opportunity in all aspects of our work. T he successful candidate for this faculty position will have the experiences, knowledge, and skills to build their pedagogy, curriculum, and service in ways that reflect and enhance this commitment. Using the job announcement for this position, please list and explain up to three areas of responsibility you find as related to fulfilling this mission. Curriculum vitae Teaching statement that describes your teaching experience and philosophy, which may incorporate experience from formal or informal teaching and mentoring opportunities. Names, addresses, and contact information of at least three references who can address your history of and potential for excellence in teaching and service to be collected in the system at a later time in the recruitment process. Inquiries should be directed to : Dr. Dee Posey | deeposey@wsu.edu External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Pullman-WA/Fiscal-Specialist-1_R-15337": {
      "title": "Fiscal Specialist 1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: September 17, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 151E-YN_CS_NPS - Fiscal Specialist 1 Business Title: Fiscal Specialist 1 Employee Type: Classified Position Details: The Opportunity:   The Office of Research at Washington State University (WSU) is responsible for advancing the research enterprise at WSU systemwide. The Office of Research facilitates all aspects of the research from pre-award to compliance, advancement, development, and commercialization. The Office of Research amplifies WSU's land-grant mission by partnering with the university community, industry leaders, and other stakeholders to advance, extend, and grow the positive impact of WSU research for the state, region, and nation. Summary of Duties: Under general supervision the Fiscal Specialist 1 performs a variety of fiscal and administrative functions for the entire Office of Research area. The primary functions include maintaining and modifying fiscal records & IP databases; tracking and maintaining records related to internally funded innovation projects, invoicing clients for income and reimbursements; receiving, reviewing, and recording all incoming payments; maintaining and purchasing office supplies; reconciling monthly purchasing cards and travel card; preparing specialized financial reports; performing fiscal tasks in Workday, and other clerical duties as assigned. The Fiscal Specialist 1 will exercise independent judgement to interpret and apply principles of established procedures; independently advise staff regarding applicable policies; and make recommendations to improve efficiency.  55% Fiscal Support 25% Intellectual Property(IP) Data Management 15% Business Operations 5% Other Additional Information: This is a full-time (100 % FTE), permanent position. This position is overtime eligible. Monthly Salary: $3,653 to $4,866 | Range 40 (Steps A-M) | Successful candidates are typically hired at the beginning of the salary range and receive scheduled salary increment increases in accordance with WAC 357-28 . In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts; training and development; and employee tuition waiver. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for Classified staff and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications: Three years of fiscal record keeping experience; OR equivalent education/experience Demonstrated experience with spreadsheets Experience working with databases Demonstrated computer skills, including the ability to use office software such as Word, PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook, and/or Web Browsers Demonstrated organizational skills and attention to detail Preferred Qualifications: Experience with researching and interpreting policies and procedures Experience with WSU Administrative systems ​ Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship About Department/College/Area/ Campus - For more information about the great work we are doing and to view our mission and values, please visit our website: Washington State University | Office of Research . Area/College: Office of Research   Department Name: Office of Commercialization Location: Pullman, WA Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Position Term: 12 Month Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
    "https://wsu.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/WSU_Jobs/job/Pullman-WA/Director-of-Statewide-Campuses-Research-Advancement_R-15351": {
      "title": "Director of Statewide Campuses Research Advancement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nOnline applications must be received before 11:59pm on: October 13, 2026 If a date is not listed above, review the Applicant Instructions below for more details. Available Title(s): 1155-NN_ADMINPRO - Director Business Title: Director of Statewide Campuses Research Advancement Employee Type: Admin. Professional Position Details: The Opportunity:   The Office of Research at Washington State University (WSU) is responsible for advancing the research enterprise at WSU systemwide. The Office of Research facilitates all aspects of the research from pre-award to compliance, advancement, development, and commercialization. The Office of Research amplifies WSU's land-grant mission by partnering with the university community, industry leaders, and other stakeholders to advance, extend, and grow the positive impact of WSU research for the state, region, and nation. The Director of Statewide Campuses Research Advancement plays a central role in implementing and advancing Washington State University’s (WSU) research strategy across all statewide campuses. Reporting to the Associate Vice President for Research Advancement & Strategy and serving as a liaison to statewide campus leadership with a dotted line to the EVP for Statewide Campuses.  This position is responsible for leading efforts to harmonize research activities and needs across WSU’s statewide campuses in Everett, Tri-Cities, and Vancouver—ensuring that distinctive campus strengths are preserved while being strategically connected to build a more coordinated, competitive, vibrant and visible research ecosystem. This role facilitates alignment of research strategies, infrastructure, compliance and faculty engagement across campuses to support major interdisciplinary and transdisciplinary initiatives, strategic events, institutional research goals, and innovation and entrepreneurship programs in priority areas such as energy and environment, biofuels, sustainable aviation, agriculture, health, and emerging technologies. The Director serves as a primary connector between campuses, the Office of Research, and other institutional partners including External Affairs and Government Relations to expand participation in large-scale proposals, enhance research competitiveness, and amplify WSU’s statewide impact through a cohesive statewide research ecosystem consistent with the Office of Research mission to advance research from development through partnerships and impact, this role emphasizes system integration, place-based strengths, and collaborative growth across Washington. This role will require extensive in-state travel, including between WSU Campuses. Job Functions: 25% Statewide Research Strategy Integration 25% Cross-Campus Collaboration and Initiative Development 20% Research Capacity Building Across Campuses 10% Communication, Coordination, and Systems Alignment 10% Strategic Planning, Evaluation, and Reporting 5% Leadership and Supervision 5% Other Additional Information: This is a full-time (100 % FTE), permanent position. This position is overtime exempt. Monthly Salary: $10,552.90 - $16,500.00 | Commensurate with experience and qualifications In accordance with RCW 49.58.110 , the above salary reflects the full salary range for this position. Individual placement within the range is based on the candidate’s current experience, education, skills, and abilities related to the position. Benefits: WSU offers a comprehensive benefits package which includes paid sick and vacation leave; paid holidays; medical, dental, life and disability insurance package for employees and dependents; retirement; deferred compensation, optional supplemental retirement accounts; training and development; and employee tuition waiver. For additional information, please review the detailed Summary of Benefits offered by WSU for AP staff and Total Compensation . Required Qualifications: Position require a Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field and six (6) years of progressively responsible relevant experience, which has included at least three (3) years of managerial experience. Any combination of relevant education and professional experience may be substituted for the educational requirement on a year‐for‐year basis. A Master’s degree in a related field may be substituted for up to one (1) year of the required experience. Education and experience can be tailored to fit the specific organizational entity/directorial assignment. Demonstrated experience working in complex, multi-unit or multi-campus environments. Experience supporting interdisciplinary and multi-institutional research initiatives. Strong knowledge of federal, state, and foundation funding and compliance landscapes. Must have, or be able to obtain by time of hire, a valid driver’s license and meet requirements in accordance with  SPPM 7.10  and departmental driving standards. Must be able to travel extensively throughout the state. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in a relevant field and six (6) years of progressively responsible experience, including at least three (3) years of managerial experience (or equivalent combination of education/experience).  Minimum of 7 years of experience in research development, research administration, or related field. Experience at a land-grant or Research 1 university with a distributed campus system. Experience advancing research in priority domains such as energy, environment, agriculture, or advanced technologies. Demonstrated success facilitating cross-unit collaboration and organizational alignment. Experience designing and leading strategic initiatives across geographically distributed teams. Position Sponsorship Eligibility: Not eligible for work visa sponsorship About Department/College/Area/ Campus - For more information about the great work we are doing and to view our mission and values, please visit our website: Washington State University | Office of Research . Area/College: Office of Research   Department Name: Advancement and Partnerships team   Location: Pullman, WA 99164-1060 Application Instructions: Applicants must upload the following required documents to their online application. Application materials should clearly communicate how the applicant meets all required qualifications and additional requirements. 1) Resume 2) Cover Letter responding to position description External candidates , upload all documents in the “Application Document” section of your application. Current WSU Employees (internal candidates) , before starting your Workday application, please use these instructions to update your education and experience in your worker profile in Workday . Internal candidates, upload all documents in the “Resume/Cover Letter” section of your application. Documents may be submitted as one file or separate files. Applicants are encouraged to upload as a PDF, if possible. Reference contact information will be requested later in the recruitment process through Workday. Background Check: This position has been designated by the department to require a background check because it requires access to children or vulnerable adults as defined by RCW 74.34 , engages in law enforcement, requires security clearance, interacts with WSU students in a counseling or advising capacity, has access to personal identifying and/or financial information, unsupervised access to university buildings/property, or other business-related need. A background check will not be completed until an initial determination of qualification for employment has been made. Time Type: Full time Position Term: 12 Month Washington State University encourages all qualified candidates to apply, including members of the military and veterans, and persons with disabilities. WSU employs only U.S. citizens and lawfully authorized non-U.S. citizens. All new employees must show employment eligibility verification as required by the U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services. WSU is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in its services, programs, activities, education and employment for individuals with disabilities. To request disability accommodation in the application process, contact Human Resource Services: 509-335-4521 (v), Washington State TDD Relay Service: Voice Callers: 1-800-833-6384; TDD Callers: 1-800-833-6388, 509-335-1259(f), or hrs@wsu.edu . Notice of Non-Discrimination In matters of admission, employment, housing or services, or in the educational programs or activities it operates, WSU does not discriminate or permit discrimination by any member of its community against any individual on the basis of sex, race, color, national or ethnic origin, physical disability, mental disability, sensory disability, use of a trained service animal, age, religion, creed, genetic information, marital status, sexual orientation, gender identity, protected veteran status, honorably discharged veteran, member of the military, or immigration or citizenship status except as authorized by federal or state law, regulation, or government contract. Inquiries about the application of federal and state laws and regulations (including inquiries regarding the application of Title IX, ADA/Section 504, and implementing regulations), as well as reports and complaints of discrimination and harassment, can be made verbally or in writing to WSU’s Compliance and Civil Rights, the Department of Education’s Office of Civil Rights, or both. More information, resources, and contact information are available here: https://ccr.wsu.edu/notice-of-nondiscrimination/"
    },
